      "content": "A pulsing sensation in the belly might indicate a variety of issues, some of which could also be related to kidney stones, like an infection or inflammation. Cramping and ache associated with kidney stones are common but watching over these symptoms and equipping yourself with home care guidance is critical. \n\nIbuprofen may help relieve some discomfort, but it doesn't solve the underlying issue and should only be taken following the dosage instructions on the packaging or as advised by a healthcare provider. If the pain is severe, this is not considered an emergency, but it could worsen upwards, please consult with your doctor without delay if the sensation persists or changes in nature. Do monitor your symptoms closely and see a doctor if you experience fever, persistent or worsening pain, difficulty urinating, or other abnormal behaviors. Doing so would help avoid potential complications like an infection or an obstruction that may require more urgent attention.",
